From rmh at temple.edu  Tue Mar  1 15:36:25 2005
From: rmh at temple.edu (Richard M. Heiberger)
Date: Tue, 01 Mar 2005 10:36:25 -0500
Subject: Re: Problems associated with labelling
Message-ID: <20bfa666.d6467869.82dcd00@po-d.temple.edu>

The basic idea is to distinguish the ticks and labels, and plot
them with separate calls to axis().  Don't use the log="" argument since
that is causing you trouble.  Instead take the logs yourself and control
the labels with the axis function.  This sample illustrates the idea.
If you need further help, please send a working example.  Your original
post did not define the variables.

Rich

x <- -5:6
y <- 10^x
labpows <- c("0.00001", "0.0001", "0.001", "0.01",
             "0.1", "1", "10", "100", "1000", "10000",
             "100000", "1000000")
plot(log10(y) ~ x, yaxt="n", ylab="y")
axis(2, at=log10(y), labels=labpows, adj=1, ticks=FALSE) ##labels
axis(2, at=log10(y), labels=F) ## ticks

