I'd like to thank Richard Heiberger, Gerald Jean, Sarah Goslee, Bill Dunlap, and lastly Terry Therneau for their solutions. Trick is to use apply(), 

 

subs <- apply(is.na(tmp), 1, function(x) !any(x))
tmp[subs,]

A one-liner solution is,

 

data[apply(data, 1, FUN = function(x) !any(is.na(x))), ]

 

Even simpler is the use of na.omit() which I didn't know exist. 

 

newdata <- na.omit(old)

 

Thanks all.

 

Horace 

