I would discourage using apply() to determine rows of a data frame
with missing values.  It is faster to use na.omit() or the combination
of rowSums and is.na.

x _ matrix(1.0, 10000, 100)  # 10K rows, 100 columns
for(i in 20:60) x[i + 100 * 1:50, i] _ NA  # missing in cols 20-60, 50 rows each
> sys.time(x[apply(x, 1, FUN = function(x) !any(is.na(x))), ])
[1] 5.69 6.86
> sys.time(na.omit(x))
[1] 0.85 0.86
> sys.time(x[rowSums(is.na(x)) == 0,])
[1] 1.08 1.25

Tim Hesterberg

