Subject: Re: conditional or paired logisitic regression
Message-ID: <200503032056.j23KuFl13192@nightingale.hcp.med.harvard.edu>

Nicky Koper wrote:
> I wondered if anyone could give me information on doing paired or
> conditional logistic regression in Splus. I can't seem to figure out how
> to do it using the "help" menu. This is actually for a student of mine to
> use, so it would be helpful (but not critical) if it could be done using
> the drop-down menu.  I am using 6.2.

Conditional logistic regression is equivalent to a stratified Cox
proportional hazards model, if you set up the data in the right way.
Hence in various software, e.g. SAS, S-Plus, you can use PH software to
fit these models.  Terry Therneau had a message about this on this list a
few weeks ago; you can search the archive to find it.

