From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Tue Mar 22 19:22:30 2005
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian Ripley)
Date: Tue, 22 Mar 2005 19:22:30 +0000
Subject: Re: generic function - number of parameters
In-Reply-To: <42406F24.8080304@uvm.edu>
References: <42406F24.8080304@uvm.edu>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.61.0503221918270.31029@gannet.stats>

On Tue, 22 Mar 2005, Kristian Omland wrote:

> Hi all,
>
> Is there a generic function that returns the number of estimated parameters
> in a fitted model object?
> Or is there a component of a fitted model object that is (or includes) the
> number of parameters that was estimated?
>
> For models fit by least squares, does this work?
>   model$rank + 1
> Even if it does, surely there is a more elegant way to count them!

No, since it is immaterial to the fit if sigma^2 is estimated or not.
In short, the fit does not of itself tell you.

You can make some assumptions, and extractAIC (MASS) does so to calculate 
AIC.  So it is the nearest thing to an answer to your question that I know 
of.

