Of those two ways, the solution involving colSums takes half the time.
It operates on the whole object, whereas apply loops (internally)
over a column at a time.

n = 1000
m = matrix(1, n, n)
m[ sample(1:n^2, n) ] = 0
sys.time(a = m[ , colSums(m==0) == 0, drop=F])
sys.time(a = m[ , apply(m, 2, function(col) sum(col==0) == 0), drop=F])
# .140 seconds for colSums, .313 for apply

