Lina,

One way to get a list of all S-PLUS functions is to run

        objects("*", classed="function")

Oops.  Make that 

        objects("*", classes="function")

Beware, there are lots of them.  

Perhaps more useful is to use the "regexpr.pattern" of 
objects ("regex" for short) to look for functions that 
have names that sound like they may be of interest.  
For example:

> objects("*", regex="dup", classes="function")
$splus:
[1] "duplicated"            "duplicated.data.frame" "duplica
tedList"       

Then it becomes a simple matter to look up the help file
for each.  

Using the "regex" argument to objects() is much faster than
scanning a long listing.

Regards,

Chuck Taylor
