to get the list of all regions, do:

map(database="world", plot=F, namesonly=T)

you might want to save that in a variables as it results in a vector of
length 2284.

You can zoom in on Alaska by plotting the whole map, then use locator()
to find oposite corners of a box around the region of interest, then use
xlim and ylim like this:

map(database="world",plot=F,namesonly=T, xlim=c(-191.2,-128),
ylim=c(36,84))

which suggests that 

map("world","USA:Alaska")  

will plot what you want (maybe after applying a different orientation
and projection).

