Beth Atkinson

From greg.snow at ihc.com  Tue Mar 29 22:24:29 2005
From: greg.snow at ihc.com (Greg Snow)
Date: Tue, 29 Mar 2005 15:24:29 -0700
Subject: Re: Multiple people, 1 .Data directory
Message-ID: <s2497335.093@lp-msg1.co.ihc.com>

Don't have anyone attach the directory at position 1, everyone should
attach it at position 2 (or greater), this gives you access to the data
there, but things like .Last.value and .Random.seed will be saved in
each users local personal working directory and not interfere with the
others.  If you need to save an object to the common directory for
everyone else to use, then use the assign function rather than "<-",
everyone else should then use the sychronize function to make sure they
see the new data.

hope this helps,

