From dimitrios.rizopoulos at student.kuleuven.ac.be  Wed Mar 30 07:07:10 2005
From: dimitrios.rizopoulos at student.kuleuven.ac.be (Dimitris Rizopoulos)
Date: Wed, 30 Mar 2005 09:07:10 +0200
Subject: Re: Adaptive Gaussian Quadrature question
References: <20050329193218.25912.qmail@web50609.mail.yahoo.com>
Message-ID: <00bc01c534f7$179a93e0$0540210a@www.domain>

In GLMMs the marginal likelihood (i.e., of the observed data) involves 
an integral that cannot be solved analytically. Adaptive Gauss-Hermite 
provides an **approximation** to this integral, so strictly speaking 
you work with an approximation to the observed-data likelihood. To my 
knowledge SAS proc nlmixed and the `glme(..., method="AGQUAD")' 
function in correlatedData should do the same thing.

I hope it helps.

Best,
Dimitris

